  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Power from Pain" id="1e2c-c2a1-01ab-b553" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Drukhari grow stronger as the battle goes on and the suffering builds. Units with this rule gain the benefits below, from the game turn shown onward: Game turn: Benefit. 1: Feel No Pain (6+), or improve an existing Feel No Pain by 1. 2: May re-roll one die when rolling charge distance. 3: Furious Charge (1), or increase an existing Furious Charge (X) by 1. 4 onward: Fearless.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Combat Drugs" id="3870-8035-6b4d-b0ac" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Before deployment, roll once on this table for each unit with Combat Drugs (or choose, for +5 points per unit). The result applies to the unit for the whole game. D6: Drug, Effect. 1: Adrenalight, +1 Attack. 2: Grave Lotus, +1 Strength. 3: Hypex, +2 to the Movement Characteristic. 4: Painbringer, Improve Feel No Pain by 1. 5: Serpentin, +1 Weapon Skill. 6: Splintermind, +1 Ballistic Skill and Initiative.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drukhari Skimmers" id="1aa3-0e26-5971-64cf" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Drukhari vehicles have the Antigrav, Fast and Open-topped sub-types† unless their entry says otherwise, and may move over other models and terrain as long as they do not end on top of them.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Monstrous Creature" id="629e-4b8b-745d-12b4" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>A living war-beast with Toughness and Wounds instead of Armour Values. A Monstrous Creature is a model of the Infantry unit type with the official 2.0 Monstrous sub-type: its unit cannot be Pinned; it may fire all of its weapons in each Shooting Attack, including Reactions; it may fire Heavy and Ordnance weapons and count as Stationary even if it moved, and may still declare a charge after shooting; and no model that is not also Monstrous may join its unit. Monstrous Creatures also have Hammer of Wrath (1).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Night Vision" id="bb43-b436-18ab-1c61" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>The unit ignores the effects of Night Fighting†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealth" id="bed8-2ae0-01e6-b91d" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>If the model has not moved this turn, it cannot be targeted by ranged attacks from more than 12" away.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Obsession (X)" id="3bf4-f7e6-59c2-d363" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>When building an army, choose one obsession for each detachment. Every unit in that detachment gains Obsession (X), where X is the chosen Kabal, Cult or Coven. Unique characters may join any obsession, except Lelith Hesperax (Cult of Strife), Drazhar (any Kabal) and Urien Rakarth (Prophets of Flesh).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
